WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.357
You may hear modern data described using the three Vs: volume, velocity, and variety.

00:00:03.357 --> 00:00:06.537
Volume is about scale. Velocity is about how quickly data arrives or must be processed.

00:00:06.537 --> 00:00:08.537
Variety is about the different forms of data.

00:00:08.537 --> 00:00:10.032
This module focuses mainly on variety.

00:00:10.032 --> 00:00:11.822
But in real systems, all three interact.

00:00:11.822 --> 00:00:13.017
A small JSON file and a streaming feed of millions of JSON events may use the same format

00:00:13.017 --> 00:00:16.067
but require very different engineering solutions.

00:00:16.067 --> 00:00:19.172
Connect this idea to an e-commerce team preparing customer, purchase, and web-event data.

00:00:19.172 --> 00:00:22.432
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:22.432 --> 00:00:27.167
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:27.167 --> 00:00:28.982
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:28.982 --> 00:00:31.813
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
